  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="67854e34-0b90-53e5-a1dc-31d9f7f16fb5" activityNameId="4e89d100-3718-5726-80f3-e3a63244a466" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Wood, cork oak, under bark, u=70%, at forest road</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Wood, cork oak, under bark, u=70%, at forest road
the volume of wood produced refers to the wood not including the bark. The multi-output process "cork, harvesting / thinning / final cutting, under bark delivers the two coproducts "wood, cork oak, under bark, u=70%, at forest road" and "raw cork, at forest road". The allocation is based on the over-all revenue of wood and cork production.;
UUID: 6458179a-ebe6-31b1-9553-feff6416cc0f
Includes manual harvesting of the cork (every 10 years) and motor-manual processes for thinning and final cutting of the trees. Also included are the transport of the workers to the forests for harvesting cork and the transport of the products to the nearest forest road.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The harvesting of wood considers the motor-manual processes for "Buche, II. Ertragsklasse, starke Durchforstung"
Time period: cork yield data from 1993
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see geography and technology
Uncertainty adjustments: the assumption that German wood harvesting data are representative for Europe is considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6458179a-ebe6-31b1-9553-feff6416cc0f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
